      },
      "message": "feat(pocket): pre-drilled entry - plunge down proved drilled holes\n\nFirst slice of #1449. A 2D Pocket with links.approach.predrilled on\nenters each level by a straight plunge down a hole a Drill operation\nahead of it in the same setup made, where the hole is proved: the\ndrill is at least the tool plus 0.1 mm clearance a side, and the prior\nstock grid holds no material over the tool disc above the level (the\ncounted depth is the deeper of the grid and the drill point's cone).\nThe pass plan is re-seated on the hole so the cut leaves it by the\nshortest, provable link. Every other case keeps the asked helix, ramp\nor arc and names why. The flag on any other kind is refused at the\ndoor. It rides EditOperationParams (undo/redo) and the MCP params patch.\n\nRefs #1449\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
